# Lab database seed is part of common init (hard rule)

Agents that run `db-init --confirm` (or any destructive offline-schema
reset) **must not** leave demo logon broken. Lab fixtures live in
`pim-offline-server` `src/lab_dev_seed/` and run from:

1. `db-init` after migrations (default when `COMPLIANCE_PROFILE=lab-dev`)
2. Daemon startup `ensure_on_startup` on the same profile

Do **not** invent a new PowerShell-only seed step. Document switches in
`pim-offline-server/docs/dev/db-init-and-lab-seed.md`. Production
profiles (`cmmc-l2` / `commercial`) never auto-seed demo passwords.

Lab seed must also keep `/login` operable: merge private-network
threat-intel suppress overrides, and force `IAM_RADIUS_ENABLED=false`
unless the operator is deliberately testing RADIUS (re-enable after).
